= Checking <sec-checking>

While you write, the program helps without getting in your way. The check in the right sidebar lays out spelling and grammar of the open sheet as a list; the places are underlined in the text, and a click shows suggestions. The dictionary belongs to the project, so your own technical terms are quickly added. The check runs on your computer, and no text leaves it.

With a right click on a word you open the synonyms in the form the sentence needs: "results" gives "outcomes", not "outcome". The search in that window takes other words too, and a click replaces the word in the text.

== Keeping an overview <sec-overview>

The outline shows all headings in the order of the document, numbered as the template numbers them; skipped levels are marked. The statistics summarize the first lines of all sheets. And search (Cmd+F) finds in the sheet as you expect.
